    <item>
      <title>Definitive First Person View</title>
      <author>bubbabushido</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/720730</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/720730#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">8bbd7a49658d1e2914d78ce18d0487952a21363f</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:17:47 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab6d26d25e9a.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab778791ecd6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab778794a048.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab778798501c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Definitive First Person&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: Fixed head rendering regression&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: Implemented a proper climbing methodology&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;# BOTW First Person v1.4.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;First-person gameplay for The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild on Cemu, with an animated eye-level camera, visible player and equipment, enemy lock-on, and a custom stamina HUD.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Features&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Animated eye-position camera, 8 cm forward offset, and 90° horizontal FOV at 16:9 (approximately 58.7° vertical).&lt;br&gt;- Visible body and equipment, with head-material visibility controlled by the active scene camera and event state.&lt;br&gt;- Shield guard pose tuned for first person: the shield sits in front of you and stays visible while guarding.&lt;br&gt;- Close objects stay solid: the first-person camera uses a 10 cm near clip, so shields, boulders and other nearby geometry no longer clip away.&lt;br&gt;- Camera pulls back 10 cm while pushing boulders, so you don't end up inside them.&lt;br&gt;- Body yaw follows the view during ordinary movement. Climbing retains native body orientation and animation.&lt;br&gt;- Native enemy lock-on with first-person eye placement.&lt;br&gt;- Native bow-arm animation with the original 20° stance alignment and an 8 cm camera-right aiming-body offset, keeping hand and bow together.&lt;br&gt;- Stamina wheel beside the hearts, at 75% scale; approximately 7.5 screen pixels from the leftmost heart at 1920×1080. Gap scales with HUD resolution. Original-position preset also available.&lt;br&gt;- Sheikah Slate camera/scope adjustments; fixed-FOV first-person bow cameras without bow zoom.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.4.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fixes the shield disappearing (or only appearing when looking down) while guarding. The cause was the game's dynamic near clip plane (about 0.7–1.0 m); the main first-person camera now uses 10 cm. Shadows and other cameras keep their native values.&lt;br&gt;- Fixes seeing through boulders and other close objects for the same reason.&lt;br&gt;- Guarding shifts the body 10 cm forward along the view, keeping hand and shield together; the camera stays in place.&lt;br&gt;- Fixed left-arm guard pose (from the game's own shield-guard animation) for a stable shield position.&lt;br&gt;- Equipped items (weapons, shield, bow, nocked arrow) skip the frustum-plane stage of the game's per-model view culling while in first person, avoiding pop-out at screen edges near the camera.&lt;br&gt;- 10 cm camera pull-back while pushing boulders.&lt;br&gt;- Tunable values are grouped in `patch_Live.asm` with documented offsets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Compatibility&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tested on **Cemu 2.6, Ubuntu, Wii U EUR BOTW v208**.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Title ID: `00050000101C9500`&lt;br&gt;- Executable module hash: `0x6267BFD0`&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This package targets that version and region. Other versions/regions and operating systems have not been verified. No mod manager or BetterVR runtime is required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Install or update&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Close Cemu.&lt;br&gt;2. Back up and remove any older `00_FirstPersonView_ZoomFix` folder from Cemu's `graphicPacks` directory.&lt;br&gt;3. Extract this ZIP and copy its `00_FirstPersonView_ZoomFix` folder into `graphicPacks`.&lt;br&gt;   On the tested Linux setup: `~/.local/share/Cemu/graphicPacks/`.&lt;br&gt;4. Enable **The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild → Graphics → First Person View + Zoom Fix** in Cemu's Graphic Packs settings.&lt;br&gt;5. Select **Beside hearts** for the custom stamina position and launch BOTW.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Use only one copy of this pack. Disable other camera replacements and stamina-position patches that modify the same features. Restart the game after updating the files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To uninstall, disable this graphic pack and restart Cemu.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Notes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Shield visibility while guarding and boulder pushing were confirmed in gameplay on the tested setup. Hair visibility in the guard pose, real-time cutscenes, climbing view limits, and full-game/outfit coverage have not been fully verified; clipping or camera edge cases may remain. A 10 cm near clip slightly reduces depth precision compared with native.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Native arrow firing and gameplay logic remain in control of the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Texture upscales, lighting mods, shaders, controller profiles, streaming automation, emulator, and full game files are not included. This is not stereoscopic VR output.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Credits and notices&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Original First Person View: **MelonSpeedruns, SushiiZ, and SilentVerge**. Original attribution README included as `README-original-FPV.txt`; its three-FOV-variant description refers to the original release.&lt;br&gt;- Native body/camera and equipment work uses layout research and hook techniques from **Crementif's BotW-BetterVR**. Its MIT notice is included as `LICENSE-BetterVR.txt`.&lt;br&gt;- Stamina implementation used Cemu community graphic-pack GUI/aspect-ratio patches as a reference.&lt;br&gt;- The fixed guard-arm rotations are frame-0 values derived from the game's own `Shield_Guard_Wait` animation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The original FPV archive did not include a separate license. Attribution and the BetterVR notice are preserved; no blanket license is asserted over third-party or game-derived material. Redistribution permission for those components has not been independently verified.</description>
